    {
      "date": "1909",
      "kind": "construction",
      "description": "Holy Trinity Cathedral was built at the Van Ness Avenue corner in 1909 as the replacement for the Powell Street cathedral lost in 1906, in an eclectic style combining Russian elements — gilded finials and crosses, a main dome and a polygonal minor dome — with American Period Revival detail. A parish house was built alongside it at the same time. The architect is not recorded.",
      "source": "russian-american-context-statement"
